From 1822b366b967c93591242cb48f0fd0c8bc8e04f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiro <chiro2001@163.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 20:36:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 251/254] fix(u2b): refresh the measured envelope to 1067,
 refuse bools, mirror the report snapshot check

- measured_deviation_by_k[133144] 966 -> 1067: verify-0042-u2b-r2 extension scans of the same generator family (seeds 1001-6000 max 1067 seed 1591, seeds 6001-12000 max 1043 seed 6323; K=16696 stays 75 over 12000 seeds).  measurement_scope records both extension scans, keeps observations_are_not_a_bound=true and upper_bound.status=not_provided; no bound language is introduced.
- _check_codes refuses Python bools again (code_not_integer, same field/index semantics, output untouched) instead of silently reinterpreting True/False as 1/0.  The fast path keeps one array('b', values) conversion + one memchr for -128 and adds a single C-level set(map(type, ...)) pass (~0.05s per 8.4M elements); buffer-backed containers skip it, non-integer containers still use the strict per-element fallback.
- report-side symmetry: a measured_snapshot envelope must carry measured_deviation_by_k (report_field_missing) and a bounded kind must carry deviation_bound_by_k, mirroring the plan-side validator.
- tests: extension witnesses (133144/1591->1067, 133144/6323->1043, 16696/8410->75), bool refusal at any index + end-to-end injected-bool refusal with output untouched, report snapshot missing observations refused (portable + vendor).
